window.DOCS["6ae530b7f82f19ef123c7a78"]={"id":"6ae530b7f82f19ef123c7a78","summary":{"title_zh":"關於議程項目 11：遺傳資源數位序列資訊之主席文本","what":"這份文件是由大會主席提出的決議草案，旨在推動遺傳資源數位序列資訊（DSI）多邊機制的運作與後續發展，包含卡利基金（Cali Fund）的營運、資金分配方式及非金錢利益分享等細節。","points":["決定在資源允許下設立特設開放式工作小組，負責進一步發展包含卡利基金在內的多邊機制，並向第十八次締約方大會提出建議。","重申卡利基金的指標性貢獻率：利用者利潤的 1%，或營收的 0.1%；並徵集其他可能繳款方式（例如依產品與服務計算）的意見，請執行秘書委託研究。","卡利基金證書可能提供法律確定性，並作為增加基金資金的途徑之一；僅有金錢貢獻的使用者方能取得該年度證書。指導委員會得於過渡期間核發年度證書，以激勵使用者貢獻。","授權指導委員會在基金募資達 1.5 億美元的條件下，於第十八次締約方大會通過分配方法前先行分配資金，該權限於大會結束時終止。資金中一半指向開發中國家（包括低度開發國家、小島嶼開發中國家及經濟轉型國家）；另一半指向原住民族與地方社區的自我認定需求，其中 90% 保留給開發中國家的原住民族與地方社區，10% 保留給已開發國家的原住民族與地方社區。","非金錢利益分享仍待進一步運作，請執行秘書徵集意見並委託研究，內容包括能力差距、非金錢利益的監測與報告方法，以及 clearing-house 的透明度要求；並說明非金錢利益分享不取代卡利基金的金錢利益分享。","邀請原住民族與地方社區參與制定資料管理與治理的教育教材，並考量 FAIR 與 CARE 原則；請資料庫託管機構於第十八次締約方大會前，向執行秘書報告其落實附件第 10 段的情形，並維持開放取用。"],"open":[]},"summaryReviewed":true,"pages":[{"p":"p001","zh":"CBD_documents/zh/6ae530b7f82f19ef123c7a78/p001.md","en":[{"t":"Agenda item 11"},{"t":"Digital sequence information on genetic resources"},{"t":"President’s text"},{"t":"Digital sequence information on genetic resources*"},{"t":"Draft decision submitted by the President"},{"t":"The Conference of the Parties,"},{"t":"Recalling decisions 15/9 of 19 December 2022 and 16/2 of 1 November 2024, Reaffirming the sovereign rights of States over their natural resources and, and recognizing that the approach to the fair and equitable benefit-sharing from the use of DSI set out in the present decision is without prejudice to national access and benefit-sharing measures and mutually-agreed terms and does not affect the rights and obligations of any Party deriving from any existing international agreement;"},{"t":"Emphasizing the importance of preserving the distinctive nature of the Cali Fund as a benefit sharing fund, ensuring transparency and accountability, and maintaining clear governance structures, institutional mandates, responsibilities and decision-making authority consistent with decision 16/2;"},{"t":"Recognizing the potential asymmetries among users, including those making limited or initial use of digital sequence information on genetic resources;"},{"t":"1.     Expresses its appreciation to the Governments of Germany, Norway and the United Kingdom of Great Britain and Northern Ireland and to the European Union for their generous financial support for the activities linked with the operationalization of the Multilateral Mechanism for the Fair and Equitable Sharing of Benefits from the Use of Digital Sequence Information on Genetic Resources, including the Cali Fund, and to the Governments of Germany and South Africa for hosting the second and third meetings of the Steering Committee, respectively;"},{"t":"2.    Takes note with appreciation of the report of the Steering Committee of the Multilateral Mechanism, including the Cali Fund;1"},{"t":"3.    Decides to establish, subject to the availability of resources, an ad hoc open-ended working group on benefit-sharing from the use of digital sequence information on genetic resources to further develop the Multilateral Mechanism, including the Cali Fund, to consider the issues expressly referred to in this decision, and to make recommendations to the Conference of the Parties for consideration at its eighteenth meeting;"},{"t":"I"},{"t":"Operations of the Cali Fund"},{"t":"Thresholds and contribution rates"},{"t":"4.     Takes note of the study on contribution rates, including implications for revenue generation and economic competitiveness, and on national and international standards for the identification of small, medium and large entities;2"},{"t":"5.   Recommends the consideration of the study mentioned in paragraph 4 above and its recommendations at the eighth meeting of Subsidiary Body on Implementation;"},{"t":"* The present document is being issued without formal editing."},{"t":"1 CBD/COP/17/6/Add.1."},{"t":"2 CBD/COP/17/INF/18"}],"blocks":[{"md":"議程項目 11\n遺傳資源數位序列資訊","html":"<p>議程項目 11<br />\n遺傳資源數位序列資訊</p>","en":[0,1]},{"md":"主席文本","html":"<p>主席文本</p>","en":[2]},{"md":"遺傳資源數位序列資訊*\n主席提交之決議草案\n締約方大會，","html":"<p>遺傳資源數位序列資訊*<br />\n主席提交之決議草案<br />\n締約方大會，</p>","en":[3,4,5]},{"md":"**回顧** 2022 年 12 月 19 日之決議 15/9 與 2024 年 11 月 1 日之決議 16/2，","html":"<p><strong>回顧</strong> 2022 年 12 月 19 日之決議 15/9 與 2024 年 11 月 1 日之決議 16/2，</p>","en":[6]},{"md":"**重申** 各國對其自然資源擁有主權權利，並**承認**本決議所載關於使用 DSI 之公平且公正利益分享方式，不損害國家取得與利益分享措施及共同商定條件之規定，亦不影響任何締約方因任何現行國際協議所衍生之權利與義務；","html":"<p><strong>重申</strong> 各國對其自然資源擁有主權權利，並<strong>承認</strong>本決議所載關於使用 DSI 之公平且公正利益分享方式，不損害國家取得與利益分享措施及共同商定條件之規定，亦不影響任何締約方因任何現行國際協議所衍生之權利與義務；</p>","en":[6]},{"md":"**強調** 維持卡利基金作為利益分享基金之獨特性、確保透明度與問責制，並維持與決議 16/2 一致之清晰治理結構、機構職權、責任與決策權之重要性；","html":"<p><strong>強調</strong> 維持卡利基金作為利益分享基金之獨特性、確保透明度與問責制，並維持與決議 16/2 一致之清晰治理結構、機構職權、責任與決策權之重要性；</p>","en":[7]},{"md":"**承認** 使用者之間可能存在不對稱性，包括對遺傳資源數位序列資訊進行有限或初步使用之使用者；","html":"<p><strong>承認</strong> 使用者之間可能存在不對稱性，包括對遺傳資源數位序列資訊進行有限或初步使用之使用者；</p>","en":[8]},{"md":"1. **對** 德國、挪威、大不列顛暨北愛爾蘭聯合王國政府以及歐盟為推動「利用遺傳資源數位序列資訊公平且公正分享利益之多邊機制」（包括卡利基金）相關活動所提供之慷慨財務支持，**表示感謝**；並**對**德國與南非政府分別主辦指導委員會第二及第三次會議，**表示感謝**；","html":"<p>1. <strong>對</strong> 德國、挪威、大不列顛暨北愛爾蘭聯合王國政府以及歐盟為推動「利用遺傳資源數位序列資訊公平且公正分享利益之多邊機制」（包括卡利基金）相關活動所提供之慷慨財務支持，<strong>表示感謝</strong>；並<strong>對</strong>德國與南非政府分別主辦指導委員會第二及第三次會議，<strong>表示感謝</strong>；</p>","en":[9]},{"md":"2. **注意到** 多邊機制（包括卡利基金）指導委員會之報告；¹","html":"<p>2. <strong>注意到</strong> 多邊機制（包括卡利基金）指導委員會之報告；¹</p>","en":[10]},{"md":"3. **決定** 在資源可用之情況下，成立一個關於利用遺傳資源數位序列資訊之利益分享特設開放式工作小組，以進一步發展包括卡利基金在內之多邊機制，審議本決議中明確提及之議題，並向締約方大會提出建議，以供其第十八次會議審議；","html":"<p>3. <strong>決定</strong> 在資源可用之情況下，成立一個關於利用遺傳資源數位序列資訊之利益分享特設開放式工作小組，以進一步發展包括卡利基金在內之多邊機制，審議本決議中明確提及之議題，並向締約方大會提出建議，以供其第十八次會議審議；</p>","en":[11,12]},{"md":"I\n卡利基金之運作\n門檻與貢獻率","html":"<p>I<br />\n卡利基金之運作<br />\n門檻與貢獻率</p>","en":[13,14]},{"md":"4. **注意到** 關於貢獻率（包括對收益產生與經濟競爭力之影響）以及關於識別小型、中型與大型實體之國家與國際標準之研究；²","html":"<p>4. <strong>注意到</strong> 關於貢獻率（包括對收益產生與經濟競爭力之影響）以及關於識別小型、中型與大型實體之國家與國際標準之研究；²</p>","en":[15]},{"md":"5. **建議** 於執行附屬機構第八次會議上，審議上述第 4 段所述之研究及其建議；","html":"<p>5. <strong>建議</strong> 於執行附屬機構第八次會議上，審議上述第 4 段所述之研究及其建議；</p>","en":[16]},{"md":"---\n* 本文件發布時尚未經過正式編輯。\n¹ CBD/COP/17/6/Add.1。\n² CBD/COP/17/INF/18。","html":"<hr />\n<ul>\n<li>本文件發布時尚未經過正式編輯。<br />\n¹ CBD/COP/17/6/Add.1。<br />\n² CBD/COP/17/INF/18。</li>\n</ul>","en":[17,18,19]}]},{"p":"p002","zh":"CBD_documents/zh/6ae530b7f82f19ef123c7a78/p002.md","en":[{"t":"President’s text on item 11"},{"t":"6.     Reaffirms the indicative rates of 1% of the profit or 0.1% of the revenue of the contributing entities using digital sequence information on genetic resources under the Multilateral Mechanism;"},{"t":"Potential additional modalities"},{"t":"7.    Invites Parties, other Governments, indigenous peoples and local communities, and relevant organizations and stakeholders to submit views and information on the potential value of additional modalities, including but not limited to proportionate contribution pathways such as a products- and services-based modality that could complement or refine the approach established in decision 16/2;"},{"t":"8.     Invites Parties, other Governments, indigenous peoples and local communities, and relevant organizations and stakeholders to submit information and their views on the term “direct and indirect use of digital sequence information on genetic resources” in the context of the Multilateral Mechanism, including the Cali Fund;"},{"t":"9.    Requests the Executive Secretary, subject to the availability of resources,"},{"t":"(a) building on paragraph 8, to commission a study on potential additional modalities, including but not limited to proportionate contribution pathways such as a products- and services-based modality that could complement or refine the approach established in decision 16/2,"},{"t":"(b)   compile and synthesize the submissions pursuant to paragraph 6,"},{"t":"(c) to make the work pursuant to 9 (a) and (b) available to the ad hoc open-ended working group for its consideration, including its linkages with the work on certificates, with a view to make recommendations to the Conference of the Parties at its eighteenth meeting; Certificates"},{"t":"10. Recognizes that Cali Fund certificates, as applied solely to the digital sequence information within the scope of the Multilateral Mechanism, has links with some of its other modalities, may provide legal certainty and predictability to entities and will be one of the important means to increase capitalization of the Cali Fund, while recalling that every monetary contribution to the Cali Fund will be acknowledged by a receipt as evidence of the financial transaction;"},{"t":"11. Clarifies that only monetary contributions made by users in line with para 7 above will entitle users to receive a Cali Fund certificate for the year to which the contribution relates, without prejudice to possible future modalities;"},{"t":"12. Takes note of the work of the Steering Committee on certificates, in particular in relation to paragraphs 15 and 26 of the annex to decision 16/2, and invites the Committee to further work on the topic, as a priority, focusing on the language, legal effect and scope, verification and issuance processes, publication, taking into account the criteria in paragraphs 9 and 10 of decision 15/9, with a view to promote legal certainty to both Parties and contributing users of the digital sequence information on genetic resources;"},{"t":"13. Invites Parties to submit information on the characteristics and elements that a Cali Fund certificate would need to operationalize paragraph 15 of the annex to decision 16/2, and the processes, if any, that would need to be undertaken at the national level to recognize or give legal effect to such certificates, including in their national legislation;"},{"t":"14. Requests the Executive Secretary to compile the information submitted pursuant to paragraph 13 above and provide it to the Steering Committee for its information and so that it may take it into account in their work on the certificates and report on it to the Conference of the Parties at its eighteenth meeting;"},{"t":"15. Supports the Steering Committee, to issue annual certificates, resulting from the work noted in paragraph 14 above for contributions to the Cali Fund, on a transitional basis, as a measure"},{"t":"2/10"}],"blocks":[{"md":"主席關於議程第 11 項之文本","html":"<p>主席關於議程第 11 項之文本</p>","en":[0]},{"md":"6.\n**再次確認**在多邊機制下，使用遺傳資源數位序列資訊之貢獻實體，其指標性費率為利潤的 1% 或營收的 0.1%；","html":"<p>6.<br />\n<strong>再次確認</strong>在多邊機制下，使用遺傳資源數位序列資訊之貢獻實體，其指標性費率為利潤的 1% 或營收的 0.1%；</p>","en":[1]},{"md":"潛在之額外模式\n7.\n**邀請**締約方、其他政府、原住民族與地方社區，以及相關組織與利害關係人，就額外模式之潛在價值提交意見與資訊，包括但不限於比例貢獻路徑，例如以產品與服務為基礎之模式，該模式可作為決議 16/2 所建立之方法之補充或完善；\n8.\n**邀請**締約方、其他政府、原住民族與地方社區，以及相關組織與利害關係人，就多邊機制（包括卡利基金）背景下「遺傳資源數位序列資訊之直接與間接利用」一詞提交資訊與其意見；\n9.\n**請求**執行秘書在資源可用的情況下，","html":"<p>潛在之額外模式<br />\n7.<br />\n<strong>邀請</strong>締約方、其他政府、原住民族與地方社區，以及相關組織與利害關係人，就額外模式之潛在價值提交意見與資訊，包括但不限於比例貢獻路徑，例如以產品與服務為基礎之模式，該模式可作為決議 16/2 所建立之方法之補充或完善；<br />\n8.<br />\n<strong>邀請</strong>締約方、其他政府、原住民族與地方社區，以及相關組織與利害關係人，就多邊機制（包括卡利基金）背景下「遺傳資源數位序列資訊之直接與間接利用」一詞提交資訊與其意見；<br />\n9.<br />\n<strong>請求</strong>執行秘書在資源可用的情況下，</p>","en":[2,3,4,5]},{"md":"(a) 根據第 8 段，委託進行一項關於潛在額外模式之研究，包括但不限於比例貢獻路徑，例如以產品與服務為基礎之模式，該模式可作為決議 16/2 所建立之方法之補充或完善；\n(b) 彙編並綜合根據第 6 段所提交之內容；\n(c) 將根據第 9 (a) 及 (b) 段所進行之工作提交予特設開放式工作小組供其審議，包括其與證明書工作之關聯，旨在向第十八次締約方大會提出建議；","html":"<p>(a) 根據第 8 段，委託進行一項關於潛在額外模式之研究，包括但不限於比例貢獻路徑，例如以產品與服務為基礎之模式，該模式可作為決議 16/2 所建立之方法之補充或完善；<br />\n(b) 彙編並綜合根據第 6 段所提交之內容；<br />\n(c) 將根據第 9 (a) 及 (b) 段所進行之工作提交予特設開放式工作小組供其審議，包括其與證明書工作之關聯，旨在向第十八次締約方大會提出建議；</p>","en":[6,7,8,9]},{"md":"證明書\n10. **認識到**卡利基金證明書（僅適用於多邊機制範圍內之數位序列資訊）與其其他部分模式具有關聯，可為實體提供法律確定性與可預測性，且將是增加卡利基金資本化之重要手段之一；同時**回顧**對卡利基金之每一筆金錢貢獻均將以收據作為財務交易之憑證予以確認；\n11. **澄清**僅有依據上述第 7 段規定由使用者所進行之金錢貢獻，方有權獲得與該貢獻所屬年度相對應之卡利基金證明書，且不影響未來可能之模式；\n12. **注意到**指導委員會關於證明書之工作，特別是關於決議 16/2 附件第 15 段與第 26 段之工作，並**邀請**委員會將此議題作為優先事項進行進一步工作，重點關注文字、法律效力與範圍、查核與核發程序、公布，並考量決議 15/9 第 9 段與第 10 段之標準，旨在促進締約方與遺傳資源數位序列資訊貢獻使用者雙方之法律確定性；\n13. **邀請**締約方提交關於卡利基金證明書為落實決議 16/2 附件第 15 段所需具備之特性與要素之資訊，以及在國家層級（包括在其國內立法中）為承認或賦予此類證明書法律效力而需要進行之程序（如有）；\n14. **請求**執行秘書彙編根據上述第 13 段所提交之資訊，並提供予指導委員會以供其參考，以便其在關於證明書的工作中予以考量，並向第十八次締約方大會進行報告；\n15. **支持**指導委員會以過渡性質，根據上述第 14 段所載之工作成果，針對卡利基金之貢獻核發年度證明書，作為一項措施","html":"<p>證明書<br />\n10. <strong>認識到</strong>卡利基金證明書（僅適用於多邊機制範圍內之數位序列資訊）與其其他部分模式具有關聯，可為實體提供法律確定性與可預測性，且將是增加卡利基金資本化之重要手段之一；同時<strong>回顧</strong>對卡利基金之每一筆金錢貢獻均將以收據作為財務交易之憑證予以確認；<br />\n11. <strong>澄清</strong>僅有依據上述第 7 段規定由使用者所進行之金錢貢獻，方有權獲得與該貢獻所屬年度相對應之卡利基金證明書，且不影響未來可能之模式；<br />\n12. <strong>注意到</strong>指導委員會關於證明書之工作，特別是關於決議 16/2 附件第 15 段與第 26 段之工作，並<strong>邀請</strong>委員會將此議題作為優先事項進行進一步工作，重點關注文字、法律效力與範圍、查核與核發程序、公布，並考量決議 15/9 第 9 段與第 10 段之標準，旨在促進締約方與遺傳資源數位序列資訊貢獻使用者雙方之法律確定性；<br />\n13. <strong>邀請</strong>締約方提交關於卡利基金證明書為落實決議 16/2 附件第 15 段所需具備之特性與要素之資訊，以及在國家層級（包括在其國內立法中）為承認或賦予此類證明書法律效力而需要進行之程序（如有）；<br />\n14. <strong>請求</strong>執行秘書彙編根據上述第 13 段所提交之資訊，並提供予指導委員會以供其參考，以便其在關於證明書的工作中予以考量，並向第十八次締約方大會進行報告；<br />\n15. <strong>支持</strong>指導委員會以過渡性質，根據上述第 14 段所載之工作成果，針對卡利基金之貢獻核發年度證明書，作為一項措施</p>","en":[10,11,12,13,14]}]},{"p":"p003","zh":"CBD_documents/zh/6ae530b7f82f19ef123c7a78/p003.md","en":[{"t":"President’s text on item 11"},{"t":"to incentivize users to contribute to the Cali Fund, and to build experience and lessons learned to be considered as part of its review by the Conference of the Parties at its eighteenth meeting; Allocation methodology"},{"t":"16. Welcomes the outcomes of the work of the of the Ad Hoc Technical Expert Group on Allocation Methodology on the disbursement of funds from the Cali Fund;3"},{"t":"17.   Takes note of the design principles for the allocation formula and its future revisions, guided by decision 16/2, namely equity, fairness and impact; efficiency; transparency and confidence; and recognizes that the methodology should reflect the contributions to conservation and sustainable use of indigenous peoples and local communities, including women and youth within those communities;"},{"t":"18. Authorizes the Steering Committee, on an exceptional basis, to allocate funding from the Cali Fund on an exceptional basis before the allocation methodology is adopted at the eighteenth meeting of the Conference of the Parties provided that capitalization reaches 150 million United States Dollars in accordance with the following provisions, which shall cease to apply upon the conclusion of that meeting, subject to the provisions in 16/2 related to national legislation:"},{"t":"(a) Regarding the half of the funding directed to developing country Parties, in particular the least developed countries and small island developing States, and Parties with economies in transition, in accordance with paragraphs 18 and 20 of the annex to decision 16/2:"},{"t":"(i)   20% allocated equally among all countries;"},{"t":"(ii) 10% allocated according to GNI per capita adjusted by the factors used in the United Nations scale of assessments formula; countries with lower adjusted GNI per capita will receive higher allocations;"},{"t":"(iii) 70% allocated according to the Benefits Index for Biodiversity as employed by the Global Environment Facility (updated data from the ninth replenishment period of the Global Environment Facility Trust Fund, at the global level);"},{"t":"(b)   In accordance with paragraph 21 of decision 16/2, 50% of the funding will be directed to the self-identified needs of indigenous peoples and local communities as follows:"},{"t":"(i) 90% of this allocation is reserved for indigenous peoples and local communities in developing countries, least developed countries, small island developing states, countries with economies in transition allocated among countries according to paragraph 18 (a) above, and"},{"t":"(ii) 10% of this allocation is reserved for indigenous peoples and local communities in developed countries."},{"t":"19. Decides, consistent with paragraph 21 of the annex to decision 16/2, to accept the proposal from the Steering Committee, thereby ensuring the ability to disburse funds to indigenous peoples and local communities through national government authorities, or by direct payments through institutions identifies by indigenous peoples and local communities, or through hybrid or context-specific arrangements, in line with national circumstances and national legislation;"},{"t":"20. Emphasizes that the allocation methodology will evolve over time as additional and new information becomes available, and recognizes that the methodology requires further technical development and refinement in accordance with the recommendations of the Ad Hoc Technical Expert Group on Allocation Methodology;"},{"t":"21.      Invites Parties to submit views on the report of the Ad Hoc Technical Expert Group as well as the allocation methodology as outlined in paragraph 16;"},{"t":"3 CBD/COP/17/6/Add.2."},{"t":"3/10"}],"blocks":[{"md":"主席關於第 11 項議題之文本","html":"<p>主席關於第 11 項議題之文本</p>","en":[0]},{"md":"以激勵使用者對卡利基金（Cali Fund）做出貢獻，並建立經驗與教訓，以作為締約方大會第十八次會議審查時的一部分；","html":"<p>以激勵使用者對卡利基金（Cali Fund）做出貢獻，並建立經驗與教訓，以作為締約方大會第十八次會議審查時的一部分；</p>","en":[1]},{"md":"分配方法論","html":"<p>分配方法論</p>","pre":"約方大會第十八次會議審查時的一部分；\n\n","en":[2]},{"md":"16. **歡迎**關於卡利基金資金撥付之分配方法論特設技術專家小組工作成果；³","html":"<p>16. <strong>歡迎</strong>關於卡利基金資金撥付之分配方法論特設技術專家小組工作成果；³</p>","en":[2]},{"md":"17. **注意到**在決議 16/2 指引下，分配公式及其未來修訂之設計原則，即：公平、公正與影響；效率；透明度與信心；並**承認**該方法論應反映原住民族與地方社區（包括該社區內之女性與青年）對保育與永續利用之貢獻；","html":"<p>17. <strong>注意到</strong>在決議 16/2 指引下，分配公式及其未來修訂之設計原則，即：公平、公正與影響；效率；透明度與信心；並<strong>承認</strong>該方法論應反映原住民族與地方社區（包括該社區內之女性與青年）對保育與永續利用之貢獻；</p>","en":[3]},{"md":"18. **授權**指導委員會在例外情況下，於分配方法論於締約方大會第十八次會議通過前，以例外方式從卡利基金中撥付資金，惟須在符合下列規定且資本額達到 1.5 億美元之情況下，該規定應在該會議結束後停止適用，並受 16/2 中與國家立法相關規定之約束：\n    (a) 關於導向開發中國家締約方（特別是低度開發國家、小島嶼開發中國家以及經濟轉型中國家）的一半資金，應根據決議 16/2 附件第 18 段與第 20 段：\n        (i) 20% 在所有國家之間平均分配；\n        (ii) 10% 根據調整後之每人國民總所得（GNI）進行分配，調整係採用聯合國攤款比例公式中所使用之因素；調整後每人國民總所得較低之國家將獲得較高之分配；\n        (iii) 70% 根據全球環境基金（GEF）所採用之生物多樣性效益指數進行分配（更新自全球環境基金信託基金第九輪增資期間之全球層級資料）；\n    (b) 根據決議 16/2 第 21 段，50% 的資金將根據原住民族與地方社區自認之需求，按如下方式導向：\n        (i) 此項分配之 90% 預留給開發中國家、低度開發國家、小島嶼開發中國家、經濟轉型中國家，以及根據上述第 18 (a) 段於各國間分配之原住民族與地方社區，以及\n        (ii) 此項分配之 10% 預留給已開發國家之原住民族與地方社區。","html":"<p>18. <strong>授權</strong>指導委員會在例外情況下，於分配方法論於締約方大會第十八次會議通過前，以例外方式從卡利基金中撥付資金，惟須在符合下列規定且資本額達到 1.5 億美元之情況下，該規定應在該會議結束後停止適用，並受 16/2 中與國家立法相關規定之約束：<br />\n    (a) 關於導向開發中國家締約方（特別是低度開發國家、小島嶼開發中國家以及經濟轉型中國家）的一半資金，應根據決議 16/2 附件第 18 段與第 20 段：<br />\n        (i) 20% 在所有國家之間平均分配；<br />\n        (ii) 10% 根據調整後之每人國民總所得（GNI）進行分配，調整係採用聯合國攤款比例公式中所使用之因素；調整後每人國民總所得較低之國家將獲得較高之分配；<br />\n        (iii) 70% 根據全球環境基金（GEF）所採用之生物多樣性效益指數進行分配（更新自全球環境基金信託基金第九輪增資期間之全球層級資料）；<br />\n    (b) 根據決議 16/2 第 21 段，50% 的資金將根據原住民族與地方社區自認之需求，按如下方式導向：<br />\n        (i) 此項分配之 90% 預留給開發中國家、低度開發國家、小島嶼開發中國家、經濟轉型中國家，以及根據上述第 18 (a) 段於各國間分配之原住民族與地方社區，以及<br />\n        (ii) 此項分配之 10% 預留給已開發國家之原住民族與地方社區。</p>","en":[4,5,6,7,8]},{"md":"19. **決定**與決議 16/2 附件第 21 段保持一致，接受指導委員會之提案，從而確保能透過國家政府機關、或透過由原住民族與地方社區指定之機構進行直接支付，或透過符合國家情況與國家立法之混合或特定情境安排，向原住民族與地方社區撥付資金；","html":"<p>19. <strong>決定</strong>與決議 16/2 附件第 21 段保持一致，接受指導委員會之提案，從而確保能透過國家政府機關、或透過由原住民族與地方社區指定之機構進行直接支付，或透過符合國家情況與國家立法之混合或特定情境安排，向原住民族與地方社區撥付資金；</p>","en":[9,10,11,12]},{"md":"20. **強調**分配方法論將隨著更多且新資訊的取得而隨時間演進，並**承認**該方法論需根據分配方法論特設技術專家小組之建議，進行進一步的技術開發與精煉；","html":"<p>20. <strong>強調</strong>分配方法論將隨著更多且新資訊的取得而隨時間演進，並<strong>承認</strong>該方法論需根據分配方法論特設技術專家小組之建議，進行進一步的技術開發與精煉；</p>","en":[13]},{"md":"21. **邀請**締約方就特設技術專家小組之報告以及第 16 段所述之分配方法論提交意見；","html":"<p>21. <strong>邀請</strong>締約方就特設技術專家小組之報告以及第 16 段所述之分配方法論提交意見；</p>","en":[14]},{"md":"***","html":"<hr />","en":[14]},{"md":"³ CBD/COP/17/6/Add.2.","html":"<p>³ CBD/COP/17/6/Add.2.</p>","en":[15,16]}]},{"p":"p004","zh":"CBD_documents/zh/6ae530b7f82f19ef123c7a78/p004.md","en":[{"t":"President’s text on item 11"},{"t":"22. Decides to establish, subject to the availability of resources, an Ad Hoc Technical Expert Group on Allocation Methodology with the terms of reference provided in annex I, taking into account the views referred to in paragraph 21, and allowing for exchange of views between the Ad Hoc Technical Expert Group on Allocation Methodology and the Steering Committee, specifically to:"},{"t":"(a) Identify and evaluate new or updated data relevant to the allocation methodology, in particular for the calculation of allocations to targeted governments, including data and indicators generated under the Convention and the Monitoring Framework of the Kunming-Montreal Global Biodiversity Framework;"},{"t":"(b) Develop a methodology specifically for the purpose of calculating allocations to indigenous peoples and local communities, with their full and effective participation in the process, including consideration of women and youth within those communities, including the assessment of the specific distributional effects of the provisions in paragraph 18;"},{"t":"(c) Develop criterion (b) of the allocation methodology on the geographical origin of the genetic resources from which digital sequence information on genetic resources in the database was derived, including potential recognized sources of data available at the global level, such as an indicator, and as applicable, the potential need to develop a new indicator, and in all cases reporting on options for custodianship of the indicator, current or future availability, an assessment of biases and gaps, as well as a global evaluation of the need and feasibility to provide data for such a criterion;"},{"t":"(d) To provide information on its work pursuant to subparagraphs 22 (a), (b) and (c) for consideration by the Subsidiary Body on Implementation and with a view to make a recommendation to the Conference of the Parties at the eighteenth meeting so it may adopt the revised allocation methodology;"},{"t":"II"},{"t":"Non-monetary benefit sharing and data availability and accessibility"},{"t":"23. Recognises that further work is needed to operationalise the elements of the Multilateral Mechanism that address non-monetary benefit sharing and capacity building and development, acknowledges the important role they play in the effective implementation of the Mechanism and notes the need for adequate funding to support such activities, in line decision 16/2;"},{"t":"24.     Requests the Executive Secretary, subject to the availability of resources, to:"},{"t":"(a) Invite Parties, other Governments, indigenous peoples and local communities, and relevant organizations and stakeholders to share views, information, and on-going work on digital sequence information on genetic resources non-monetary benefit-sharing including, inter alia, best practices, practical options for enhancing the delivery, accessibility and effectiveness of non-monetary benefits, particularly for developing country Parties, including least developed countries and small island developing States, projects and methods for quantifying and demonstrating non-monetary benefit-sharing;"},{"t":"(b) Commission a study, under the guidance of the Steering Committee, on current non-monetary benefit-sharing by all users of digital sequence information on genetic resources in order to identify, inter alia:"},{"t":"(i)     capacity gaps in accessing, using and generating such digital sequence information, including needs for the development of sustained scientific and technological capacities, pathways for the self-assessment of capacity needs;"},{"t":"(ii)    methods to monitor and report non-monetary benefits;"},{"t":"(iii)   examples of the successful delivery of targeted non-monetary benefits, including through the network of regional and subregional technical and scientific cooperation support centres, including non-monetary benefits arising from the use of digital"},{"t":"4/10"}],"blocks":[{"md":"主席關於第 11 項議程之文本","html":"<p>主席關於第 11 項議程之文本</p>","en":[0]},{"md":"22. **決定**在資源可用的情況下，根據附件 I 所提供的任務說明，考慮第 21 段所述之意見，並允許分配方法論特設技術專家小組與指導委員會之間進行意見交換，成立一個分配方法論特設技術專家小組，特別是為了：\n(a) 識別並評估與分配方法論相關的新型或更新之資料，特別是針對向目標政府分配額度之計算，包括在《公約》及《昆明－蒙特婁全球生物多樣性綱要》監測架構下所產生的資料與指標；\n(b) 制定一項專門用於計算向原住民族與地方社區分配額度之方法論，並使其充分且有效地參與該過程，包括考量該社區內之女性與青年，以及評估第 18 段規定之特定分配影響；\n(c) 針對分配方法論之標準 (b) 進行開發，即關於資料庫中遺傳資源數位序列資訊所衍生之遺傳資源地理來源，包括全球層級可取得之潛在公認資料來源（例如一項指標），以及在適用情況下，開發新指標之潛在需求，且在所有情況下，皆須報告關於指標保管之選項、目前或未來之可用性、偏差與差距之評估，以及針對提供該標準所需資料之需求與可行性進行全球性評估；\n(d) 就其根據第 22 (a)、(b) 及 (c) 分段所進行之工作提供資訊，供執行附屬機構審議，並旨在於第十八次締約方大會提出建議，以便其採納修訂後之分配方法論；","html":"<p>22. <strong>決定</strong>在資源可用的情況下，根據附件 I 所提供的任務說明，考慮第 21 段所述之意見，並允許分配方法論特設技術專家小組與指導委員會之間進行意見交換，成立一個分配方法論特設技術專家小組，特別是為了：<br />\n(a) 識別並評估與分配方法論相關的新型或更新之資料，特別是針對向目標政府分配額度之計算，包括在《公約》及《昆明－蒙特婁全球生物多樣性綱要》監測架構下所產生的資料與指標；<br />\n(b) 制定一項專門用於計算向原住民族與地方社區分配額度之方法論，並使其充分且有效地參與該過程，包括考量該社區內之女性與青年，以及評估第 18 段規定之特定分配影響；<br />\n(c) 針對分配方法論之標準 (b) 進行開發，即關於資料庫中遺傳資源數位序列資訊所衍生之遺傳資源地理來源，包括全球層級可取得之潛在公認資料來源（例如一項指標），以及在適用情況下，開發新指標之潛在需求，且在所有情況下，皆須報告關於指標保管之選項、目前或未來之可用性、偏差與差距之評估，以及針對提供該標準所需資料之需求與可行性進行全球性評估；<br />\n(d) 就其根據第 22 (a)、(b) 及 (c) 分段所進行之工作提供資訊，供執行附屬機構審議，並旨在於第十八次締約方大會提出建議，以便其採納修訂後之分配方法論；</p>","en":[1,2,3,4,5]},{"md":"II\n非貨幣性利益分享與資料之可用性及可取得性","html":"<p>II<br />\n非貨幣性利益分享與資料之可用性及可取得性</p>","en":[6,7]},{"md":"23. **認識到**需要進一步的工作以使處理非貨幣性利益分享及能力建構與發展之多邊機制要素具備可操作性，**承認**其在該機制有效執行中所扮演的重要角色，並**注意到**需要充足的資金以支持此類活動，此與決議 16/2 一致；","html":"<p>23. <strong>認識到</strong>需要進一步的工作以使處理非貨幣性利益分享及能力建構與發展之多邊機制要素具備可操作性，<strong>承認</strong>其在該機制有效執行中所扮演的重要角色，並<strong>注意到</strong>需要充足的資金以支持此類活動，此與決議 16/2 一致；</p>","en":[8]},{"md":"24. **請求**執行秘書在資源可用的情況下：","html":"<p>24. <strong>請求</strong>執行秘書在資源可用的情況下：</p>","en":[9]},{"md":"(a) **邀請**締約方、其他政府、原住民族與地方社區，以及相關組織與利害關係人，分享關於遺傳資源數位序列資訊非貨幣性利益分享之意見、資訊及進行中之工作，包括（除其他事項外）最佳實務、增進非貨幣性利益之交付、可取得性與有效性之務實選項（特別是針對開發中國家締約方，包括低度開發國家與小島嶼開發中國家）、量化與證明非貨幣性利益分享之專案與方法；\n(b) 在指導委員會之指導下，委託進行一項關於所有遺傳資源數位序列資訊使用者目前非貨幣性利益分享之研究，以識別（除其他事項外）：","html":"<p>(a) <strong>邀請</strong>締約方、其他政府、原住民族與地方社區，以及相關組織與利害關係人，分享關於遺傳資源數位序列資訊非貨幣性利益分享之意見、資訊及進行中之工作，包括（除其他事項外）最佳實務、增進非貨幣性利益之交付、可取得性與有效性之務實選項（特別是針對開發中國家締約方，包括低度開發國家與小島嶼開發中國家）、量化與證明非貨幣性利益分享之專案與方法；<br />\n(b) 在指導委員會之指導下，委託進行一項關於所有遺傳資源數位序列資訊使用者目前非貨幣性利益分享之研究，以識別（除其他事項外）：</p>","en":[10,11]},{"md":"(i) 取得、使用及產生此類數位序列資訊之能力差距，包括對於發展持續性科學與技術能力之需求，以及能力需求自我評估之路徑；","html":"<p>(i) 取得、使用及產生此類數位序列資訊之能力差距，包括對於發展持續性科學與技術能力之需求，以及能力需求自我評估之路徑；</p>","en":[12]},{"md":"(ii) 監測與報告非貨幣性利益之方法；","html":"<p>(ii) 監測與報告非貨幣性利益之方法；</p>","en":[13]},{"md":"(iii) 成功交付目標非貨幣性利益之範例，包括透過區域與次區域技術及科學合作支援中心網絡，包括因使用屬於多邊機制範圍內之遺傳資源數位序列資訊所產生之非貨幣性利益；","html":"<p>(iii) 成功交付目標非貨幣性利益之範例，包括透過區域與次區域技術及科學合作支援中心網絡，包括因使用屬於多邊機制範圍內之遺傳資源數位序列資訊所產生之非貨幣性利益；</p>","en":[14,15]}]},{"p":"p005","zh":"CBD_documents/zh/6ae530b7f82f19ef123c7a78/p005.md","en":[{"t":"President’s text on item 11"},{"t":"sequence information on genetic resources within the scope of the Multilateral Mechanism;"},{"t":"(iv)   overview of whether and how the same issues are being considered under other international access and benefit sharing agreements with due consideration of capacity-building, technology transfer, scientific cooperation and the development of national capacities to generate, manage, access and utilize digital sequence information on genetic resources;"},{"t":"(v)    ways in which non-monetary benefit contributions from the Multilateral Mechanism can be integrated into reporting as part of the monitoring framework for the Kunming- Montreal Global Biodiversity Framework;"},{"t":"(vi)   requirements and further work needed on the clearing house for the Multilateral Mechanism provided for in paragraph 8 of the annex to decision 16/2, including transparency and accountability in reporting non-monetary benefit sharing, and;"},{"t":"(vii) recommendations for the Steering Committee for further operationalization, recognizing that non-monetary benefit-sharing complements, and does not substitute for, monetary benefit-sharing through the Cali Fund under decision 16/2;"},{"t":"(c) Provide the Steering Committee with the outcome of the work described in subparagraph 24 (a) and (b) above for its consideration with the aim to share its views and give recommendations, and submit the outcomes of this work to the ad hoc open-ended working group for its consideration;"},{"t":"25. Invites the ad hoc open-ended working group to consider the work pursuant to paragraph 24 and submit its recommendations to the Conference of the Parties at its eighteenth meeting; Data accessibility and accountability"},{"t":"26. Invites, with the aim to making publicly available digital sequence information on genetic resources further accessible in a transparent and accountable manner:"},{"t":"(a) Indigenous peoples and local communities, including women and youth among them, to contribute, in consultation and collaboration, with Parties, and digital sequence information on genetic resources database managers, the scientific community, users of digital sequence information on genetic resources, relevant organizations and initiatives, as appropriate, to the development of educational material for use by database operators, scientific and research institutions, the Secretariat and other stakeholders, as relevant, on the management and governance of data linked with indigenous peoples and local communities, including the women and youth within those communities, and their traditional knowledge, including consideration of and alignment with the principles of findability, accessibility, interoperability and reusability (FAIR) and collective benefit, authority to control, responsibility and ethics (CARE), and collective benefit, authority to control, responsibility and ethics, and considering the recommendations set out in section III of the United Nations Educational, Scientific and Cultural Organization Recommendation on Open Science, in order to, inter alia, providing guidance for scientific publications on research using digital sequence information on genetic resources;"},{"t":"(b) Organizations hosting databases that make digital sequence information on genetic resources publicly available to share information with the Executive Secretary by the eighteenth meeting of the Conference of the Parties concerning their implementation of paragraph 10 of the annex to decision 16/2 while maintaining open access, including for making available, where known, information on the country of origin of the genetic resource from which the DSI was derived;"},{"t":"(c) Parties and other Governments funding, sponsoring or hosting sequence databases to share information on the actions that they have taken to make sure that entities operating those databases progressively implement paragraphs 11 and 12 of the annex to decision 16/2;"},{"t":"5/10"}],"blocks":[{"md":"主席關於議程第 11 項之文本","html":"<p>主席關於議程第 11 項之文本</p>","en":[0,1]},{"md":"(iv) 概述在其他國際取得與利益分享協議下，是否以及如何考慮相同議題，並應適當考量能力建構、技術轉移、科學合作，以及開發用於產生、管理、取得與利用遺傳資源數位序列資訊之國家能力；","html":"<p>(iv) 概述在其他國際取得與利益分享協議下，是否以及如何考慮相同議題，並應適當考量能力建構、技術轉移、科學合作，以及開發用於產生、管理、取得與利用遺傳資源數位序列資訊之國家能力；</p>","en":[2]},{"md":"(v) 將來自多邊機制之非貨幣性利益貢獻，以整合至報告中，作為昆明－蒙特婁全球生物多樣性綱要監測架構之一部分之方式；","html":"<p>(v) 將來自多邊機制之非貨幣性利益貢獻，以整合至報告中，作為昆明－蒙特婁全球生物多樣性綱要監測架構之一部分之方式；</p>","en":[3]},{"md":"(vi) 針對決議 16/2 附件第 8 段所規定之多邊機制資訊交換所，其所需之要求與進一步工作，包括非貨幣性利益分享報告之透明度與問責制；以及","html":"<p>(vi) 針對決議 16/2 附件第 8 段所規定之多邊機制資訊交換所，其所需之要求與進一步工作，包括非貨幣性利益分享報告之透明度與問責制；以及</p>","en":[4]},{"md":"(vii) 針對指導委員會進一步運作之建議，並承認非貨幣性利益分享係對決議 16/2 下卡利基金之貨幣性利益分享之補充，而非取代；","html":"<p>(vii) 針對指導委員會進一步運作之建議，並承認非貨幣性利益分享係對決議 16/2 下卡利基金之貨幣性利益分享之補充，而非取代；</p>","en":[5]},{"md":"(c) 將上述第 24 (a) 及 (b) 分段所述工作之結果提供予指導委員會審議，旨在分享其觀點並提出建議，並將此工作之結果提交予特設開放式工作小組審議；","html":"<p>(c) 將上述第 24 (a) 及 (b) 分段所述工作之結果提供予指導委員會審議，旨在分享其觀點並提出建議，並將此工作之結果提交予特設開放式工作小組審議；</p>","en":[6]},{"md":"25. **邀請**特設開放式工作小組就第 24 段之工作進行審議，並於第十八次締約方大會提交其建議；","html":"<p>25. <strong>邀請</strong>特設開放式工作小組就第 24 段之工作進行審議，並於第十八次締約方大會提交其建議；</p>","en":[7]},{"md":"資料可取得性與問責制","html":"<p>資料可取得性與問責制</p>","en":[7]},{"md":"26. **邀請**，旨在以透明且具問責制之方式，使公開發布之遺傳資源數位序列資訊更具可取得性：","html":"<p>26. <strong>邀請</strong>，旨在以透明且具問責制之方式，使公開發布之遺傳資源數位序列資訊更具可取得性：</p>","en":[8]},{"md":"(a) 原住民族與地方社區，包括其間之女性與青年，在適當情況下，透過與締約方、遺傳資源數位序列資訊資料庫管理員、科學界、遺傳資源數位序列資訊使用者、相關組織與倡議進行諮詢與合作，參與開發供資料庫營運者、科學與研究機構、秘書處及其他相關利害關係人使用之教育教材，內容涉及與原住民族與地方社區（包括該社區內之女性與青年）及其傳統知識相關之資料管理與治理，包括考量並符合可發現、可取得、可互操作與可重複使用（FAIR）以及集體利益、控制權、責任與倫理（CARE）之原則，並考量聯合國教育、科學及文化組織《關於開放科學之建議》第三節所列之建議，旨在（除其他事項外）為使用遺傳資源數位序列資訊進行研究之科學出版物提供指引；","html":"<p>(a) 原住民族與地方社區，包括其間之女性與青年，在適當情況下，透過與締約方、遺傳資源數位序列資訊資料庫管理員、科學界、遺傳資源數位序列資訊使用者、相關組織與倡議進行諮詢與合作，參與開發供資料庫營運者、科學與研究機構、秘書處及其他相關利害關係人使用之教育教材，內容涉及與原住民族與地方社區（包括該社區內之女性與青年）及其傳統知識相關之資料管理與治理，包括考量並符合可發現、可取得、可互操作與可重複使用（FAIR）以及集體利益、控制權、責任與倫理（CARE）之原則，並考量聯合國教育、科學及文化組織《關於開放科學之建議》第三節所列之建議，旨在（除其他事項外）為使用遺傳資源數位序列資訊進行研究之科學出版物提供指引；</p>","en":[9]},{"md":"(b) 提供遺傳資源數位序列資訊公開發布之資料庫託管組織，於第十八次締約方大會前，與執行秘書分享關於其執行決議 16/2 附件第 10 段之情況，同時維持開放取得，包括在已知情況下，提供關於該數位序列資訊所衍生之遺傳資源來源國之資訊；","html":"<p>(b) 提供遺傳資源數位序列資訊公開發布之資料庫託管組織，於第十八次締約方大會前，與執行秘書分享關於其執行決議 16/2 附件第 10 段之情況，同時維持開放取得，包括在已知情況下，提供關於該數位序列資訊所衍生之遺傳資源來源國之資訊；</p>","en":[10]},{"md":"(c) 資助、贊助或託管序列資料庫之締約方及其他政府，分享其已採取之行動資訊，以確保營運該等資料庫之實體正逐步執行決議 16/2 附件第 11 及 12 段之規定；","html":"<p>(c) 資助、贊助或託管序列資料庫之締約方及其他政府，分享其已採取之行動資訊，以確保營運該等資料庫之實體正逐步執行決議 16/2 附件第 11 及 12 段之規定；</p>","en":[11,12]}]},{"p":"p006","zh":"CBD_documents/zh/6ae530b7f82f19ef123c7a78/p006.md","en":[{"t":"President’s text on item 11"},{"t":"27. Invites Parties and relevant organizations and stakeholders in a position to do so to provide capacity-building, technical assistance, technology transfer on mutually agreed terms and financial support for the work outlined in subparagraphs 26 (a) and (b) above;"},{"t":"28. Invites the various actors referred to in paragraph 26 above to inform the Secretariat of relevant work undertaken and its results;"},{"t":"29.    Also requests the Executive Secretary, subject to the availability of resources:"},{"t":"(a) To collect the information mentioned in paragraph 36 above and disseminate it through the clearing-house mechanism of the Convention and the Access and Benefit-sharing Clearing- House;"},{"t":"(b) To issue a call for collaboration with other platforms and clearing houses outside the Convention and its Protocols on the dissemination of that information;"},{"t":"30. Requests the Executive Secretary, subject to the availability of resources, to ensure that the findings and recommendations arising from the study on tools and models, such as databases, for making digital sequence information on genetic resources publicly available and accessible in a transparent and accountable manner are subject to peer review, allowing Parties, indigenous peoples and local communities, database operators and relevant experts to provide comments, and to submit the finalized study and recommendation for review by the Ad Hoc Open Ended Working Group; III"},{"t":"Steering Committee and Governance of the Multilateral Mechanism"},{"t":"31. Welcomes the rule on the membership of the Steering Committee, including the transitional arrangements for the staggered renewal of its current membership;4"},{"t":"32. Requests the Steering Committee to add a rule to their Rules of Procedure on members selection stating that future members of the Steering Committee should be nominated by the respective regional groups and constituencies, possessing appropriate expertise, as determined by their nominating regional groups and constituencies, so as to ensure the effective exercise of the functions of the Committee;"},{"t":"33. Requests the Executive Secretary to invite each region to nominate one representative and to communicate the nomination through its respective Bureau member;"},{"t":"Operational aspects of the Multilateral Mechanism, including the Cali Fund"},{"t":"34. Recalls that the Multilateral Mechanism for the Fair and Equitable Benefit Sharing from the Use of Digital Sequence Information on Genetic Resources, including the Cali Fund, operates under the authority and guidance of and is accountable to the Conference of Parties, in accordance with decision 16/2;"},{"t":"35. Also recalls that the Cali Fund is currently administered by the United Nations through the Multi-Partner Trust Fund Office, as foreseen in decisions of the Conference of Parties at its sixteenth meeting;"},{"t":"36. Acknowledges that the ‘Standard Memorandum of Understanding to establish the partnership between United Nations Organizations’ to open a Fund administered by the Multi-Partner Trust Fund of the United Nations contains language which sets the basis of this partnership as agreed by the Members to the United Nations and approved by the UN Sustainable Development Group, and that in consequence, some adjustments may be proposed to the text to ensure its consistency with decision 16/2 and the authority and guidance of the Conference of the Parties over the Multilateral Mechanism, including the Cali Fund;"},{"t":"4 CBD/COP/17/2 item 11 annex I"},{"t":"6/10"}],"blocks":[{"md":"主席關於議程第 11 項之文本","html":"<p>主席關於議程第 11 項之文本</p>","en":[0]},{"md":"27. **邀請**締約方以及有能力之相關組織與利害關係人，針對上述第 26 (a) 及 (b) 小項所述之工作，提供能力建構、技術協助、依共同商定條件進行之技術轉移以及財務支持；","html":"<p>27. <strong>邀請</strong>締約方以及有能力之相關組織與利害關係人，針對上述第 26 (a) 及 (b) 小項所述之工作，提供能力建構、技術協助、依共同商定條件進行之技術轉移以及財務支持；</p>","en":[1]},{"md":"28. **邀請**上述第 26 段所述之各方行為者，將所開展之相關工作及其結果通報秘書處；","html":"<p>28. <strong>邀請</strong>上述第 26 段所述之各方行為者，將所開展之相關工作及其結果通報秘書處；</p>","en":[2]},{"md":"29. **同時請求**執行秘書在資源可用的情況下：","html":"<p>29. <strong>同時請求</strong>執行秘書在資源可用的情況下：</p>","en":[3]},{"md":"(a) 收集上述第 36 段所述之資訊，並透過本公約之資訊交換機制及取得與利益分享資訊交換所進行傳播；\n(b) 就該資訊之傳播，發出與本公約及其議定書之外的其他平台與資訊交換所進行合作之呼籲；","html":"<p>(a) 收集上述第 36 段所述之資訊，並透過本公約之資訊交換機制及取得與利益分享資訊交換所進行傳播；<br />\n(b) 就該資訊之傳播，發出與本公約及其議定書之外的其他平台與資訊交換所進行合作之呼籲；</p>","en":[4,5]},{"md":"30. **請求**執行秘書在資源可用的情況下，確保針對使遺傳資源數位序列資訊能以透明且負責任之方式公開且可取得之工具與模式（例如資料庫）的研究結果與建議，應經過同儕審查，以允許締約方、原住民族與地方社區、資料庫營運者及相關專家提供意見，並將定案之研究與建議提交予特設開放式工作小組審查；","html":"<p>30. <strong>請求</strong>執行秘書在資源可用的情況下，確保針對使遺傳資源數位序列資訊能以透明且負責任之方式公開且可取得之工具與模式（例如資料庫）的研究結果與建議，應經過同儕審查，以允許締約方、原住民族與地方社區、資料庫營運者及相關專家提供意見，並將定案之研究與建議提交予特設開放式工作小組審查；</p>","en":[6]},{"md":"III\n多邊機制之指導委員會與治理","html":"<p>III<br />\n多邊機制之指導委員會與治理</p>","en":[7]},{"md":"31. **歡迎**關於指導委員會成員資格之規則，包括其現有成員分階段更新之過渡安排；⁴","html":"<p>31. <strong>歡迎</strong>關於指導委員會成員資格之規則，包括其現有成員分階段更新之過渡安排；⁴</p>","en":[8]},{"md":"32. **請求**指導委員會在其議事規則中增加一項關於成員遴選之規則，規定指導委員會之未來成員應由各自之區域集團與選民團提名，並具備由其提名之區域集團與選民團所認定之適當專業知識，以確保委員會職能之有效行使；","html":"<p>32. <strong>請求</strong>指導委員會在其議事規則中增加一項關於成員遴選之規則，規定指導委員會之未來成員應由各自之區域集團與選民團提名，並具備由其提名之區域集團與選民團所認定之適當專業知識，以確保委員會職能之有效行使；</p>","en":[9]},{"md":"33. **請求**執行秘書邀請各區域提名一名代表，並透過其各自之主席團成員進行提名通報；","html":"<p>33. <strong>請求</strong>執行秘書邀請各區域提名一名代表，並透過其各自之主席團成員進行提名通報；</p>","en":[10]},{"md":"多邊機制之營運層面，包括卡利基金","html":"<p>多邊機制之營運層面，包括卡利基金</p>","en":[11]},{"md":"34. **回顧**關於利用遺傳資源數位序列資訊以實現公平且公正之利益分享之多邊機制（包括卡利基金），係根據決議 16/2，在締約方大會之權威與指導下運作，並對締約方大會負責；","html":"<p>34. <strong>回顧</strong>關於利用遺傳資源數位序列資訊以實現公平且公正之利益分享之多邊機制（包括卡利基金），係根據決議 16/2，在締約方大會之權威與指導下運作，並對締約方大會負責；</p>","en":[12]},{"md":"35. **同時回顧**卡利基金目前由聯合國透過多方信託基金辦公室進行管理，正如締約方大會第十六次會議之決議所預見；","html":"<p>35. <strong>同時回顧</strong>卡利基金目前由聯合國透過多方信託基金辦公室進行管理，正如締約方大會第十六次會議之決議所預見；</p>","en":[13]},{"md":"36. **承認**「建立聯合國組織間夥伴關係之標準合作備忘錄」旨在透過聯合國多方信託基金開設一項基金，其內容包含由聯合國會員國所同意、並經聯合國永續發展集團批准之夥伴關係基礎文字；因此，可能需對文本提出若干調整，以確保其與決議 16/2 以及締約方大會對多邊機制（包括卡利基金）之權威與指導保持一致；","html":"<p>36. <strong>承認</strong>「建立聯合國組織間夥伴關係之標準合作備忘錄」旨在透過聯合國多方信託基金開設一項基金，其內容包含由聯合國會員國所同意、並經聯合國永續發展集團批准之夥伴關係基礎文字；因此，可能需對文本提出若干調整，以確保其與決議 16/2 以及締約方大會對多邊機制（包括卡利基金）之權威與指導保持一致；</p>","en":[14]},{"md":"***","html":"<hr />","en":[14]},{"md":"⁴ CBD/COP/17/2 議程第 11 項附件 I","html":"<p>⁴ CBD/COP/17/2 議程第 11 項附件 I</p>","en":[15,16]}]},{"p":"p007","zh":"CBD_documents/zh/6ae530b7f82f19ef123c7a78/p007.md","en":[{"t":"President’s text on item 11"},{"t":"37. Also acknowledges that the signatories of the Memorandum of Understanding of the Cali Fund are the UNDP, the UNEP, and the SCBD, as an agreement with the MPTFO, and that the legal and fiduciary responsibility arising therefrom must be consistent with their respective legal frameworks;"},{"t":"38. Further acknowledges that the Multilateral Mechanism, including the Cali Fund, is to be reviewed by the Conference of the Parties at its eighteenth meeting, and that this review is inclusive of governance of the Mechanism, including the Memorandum of Understanding, its annexes and the Steering Committee’s terms of reference and modus operandi;"},{"t":"39. Considers that the Memorandum of Understanding of the Multilateral Mechanism and its annexes, including the Cali Fund should align with decision 16/2 and that the Memorandum of Understanding and its Annexes should reflect that the Cali Fund is a Fund to facilitate monetary benefit-sharing from the use of Digital Sequence Information on Genetic Resources;"},{"t":"40. Therefore calls upon the signatories of the Memorandum of Understanding of the Cali Fund to adjust terminology in the Memorandum of Understanding from donor/donations to contributor/contributions, consistent with the benefit-sharing arrangements and established under decision 16/2;"},{"t":"41. Decides to establish on an exceptional and time-bound basis, subject to the availability of resources, a legal experts group with one member, with experience on similar agreements and mechanisms, nominated by each UN region with a mandate to examine, with the support of the legal experts of United Nations Participating Organizations and the Multi-Partner Trust Fund Office,"},{"t":"42. Also decides that this group shall meet online, subject to the availability of resources, with additional online meetings as needed;"},{"t":"43.    Requests the Executive Secretary, subject to the availability of resources, to:"},{"t":"(a)    Facilitate the formation of this group through a call for nomination;"},{"t":"(b)    Support this group in its work according to the mandate in paragraph 41;"},{"t":"(c) Report the outcomes of this work to the Steering Committee of the Multilateral Mechanism, including the Cali Fund, for its technical review and comments, without prejudice to the recommendations of the legal experts group;"},{"t":"44. Considers that in order for the good functioning and capitalization of the Multilateral Mechanism including the Cali Fund, the Memorandum of Understanding as is currently drafted will continue to apply and the contributors will be duly informed about the ongoing process on MOU pursuant to this decision;"},{"t":"45. Also decides that the Steering Committee may make modifications to operational documents other than the Memorandum of Understanding in the event that it is needed to ensure their responsibilities in the functioning of the Multilateral Mechanism, without prejudice to the outcome of the work of the Legal Expert Group;"},{"t":"IV"},{"t":"Review methodology"},{"t":"46. Decides to implement the review methodology5 solely for the purpose of the first review of effectiveness of the Multilateral Mechanism, including the Cali Fund, and with a view for this methodology to be revised before the second review of effectiveness, while deciding that assumption should not be part of the methodology, but instead be assessed as part of the review;"},{"t":"5 CBD/COP/17/2 item 11 annex III"},{"t":"7/10"}],"blocks":[{"md":"主席關於第 11 項之文本","html":"<p>主席關於第 11 項之文本</p>","en":[0]},{"md":"37. 亦**注意到**卡利基金諒解備忘錄之簽署方為聯合國開發計畫署（UNDP）、聯合國環境規劃署（UNEP）及秘書處（SCBD），此為與多方信託基金事務處（MPTFO）所簽署之協議，且由此產生之法律與受託責任必須與其各自之法律框架保持一致；","html":"<p>37. 亦<strong>注意到</strong>卡利基金諒解備忘錄之簽署方為聯合國開發計畫署（UNDP）、聯合國環境規劃署（UNEP）及秘書處（SCBD），此為與多方信託基金事務處（MPTFO）所簽署之協議，且由此產生之法律與受託責任必須與其各自之法律框架保持一致；</p>","en":[1]},{"md":"38. 進一步**注意到**包括卡利基金在內之多邊機制，應由締約方大會於其第十八次會議進行審查，且此項審查應包含該機制之治理，包括諒解備忘錄、其附件以及指導委員會之職權範圍與運作方式；","html":"<p>38. 進一步<strong>注意到</strong>包括卡利基金在內之多邊機制，應由締約方大會於其第十八次會議進行審查，且此項審查應包含該機制之治理，包括諒解備忘錄、其附件以及指導委員會之職權範圍與運作方式；</p>","en":[2]},{"md":"39. **認為**多邊機制之諒解備忘錄及其附件（包括卡利基金）應與決議 16/2 保持一致，且該諒解備忘錄及其附件應反映卡利基金係一旨在促進利用遺傳資源數位序列資訊之金錢利益分享之基金；","html":"<p>39. <strong>認為</strong>多邊機制之諒解備忘錄及其附件（包括卡利基金）應與決議 16/2 保持一致，且該諒解備忘錄及其附件應反映卡利基金係一旨在促進利用遺傳資源數位序列資訊之金錢利益分享之基金；</p>","en":[3]},{"md":"40. 因此**呼籲**卡利基金諒解備忘錄之簽署方，應根據決議 16/2 所建立並與利益分享安排一致之原則，將諒解備忘錄中之術語由捐贈者／捐贈（donor/donations）調整為出資者／出資（contributor/contributions）；","html":"<p>40. 因此<strong>呼籲</strong>卡利基金諒解備忘錄之簽署方，應根據決議 16/2 所建立並與利益分享安排一致之原則，將諒解備忘錄中之術語由捐贈者／捐贈（donor/donations）調整為出資者／出資（contributor/contributions）；</p>","en":[4]},{"md":"41. **決定**在資源可用之情況下，以例外且有時限之方式，成立一個由一名成員組成之法律專家小組，成員由各聯合國區域提名，並具備類似協議與機制之經驗，其任務是在聯合國參與組織之法律專家及多方信託基金事務處之支持下，進行審查；","html":"<p>41. <strong>決定</strong>在資源可用之情況下，以例外且有時限之方式，成立一個由一名成員組成之法律專家小組，成員由各聯合國區域提名，並具備類似協議與機制之經驗，其任務是在聯合國參與組織之法律專家及多方信託基金事務處之支持下，進行審查；</p>","en":[5]},{"md":"42. 亦**決定**在資源可用之情況下，此小組應透過線上方式召開會議，並根據需要增加線上會議；","html":"<p>42. 亦<strong>決定</strong>在資源可用之情況下，此小組應透過線上方式召開會議，並根據需要增加線上會議；</p>","en":[6]},{"md":"43. **請求**執行秘書在資源可用之情況下：","html":"<p>43. <strong>請求</strong>執行秘書在資源可用之情況下：</p>","en":[7]},{"md":"(a) 透過徵求提名以促進此小組之成立；","html":"<p>(a) 透過徵求提名以促進此小組之成立；</p>","en":[8]},{"md":"(b) 根據第 41 段之任務支持此小組之工作；","html":"<p>(b) 根據第 41 段之任務支持此小組之工作；</p>","en":[9]},{"md":"(c) 將此項工作之成果提交予包括卡利基金在內之多邊機制指導委員會，以供其進行技術審查與評論，且不損害法律專家小組建議之效力；","html":"<p>(c) 將此項工作之成果提交予包括卡利基金在內之多邊機制指導委員會，以供其進行技術審查與評論，且不損害法律專家小組建議之效力；</p>","en":[10]},{"md":"44. **認為**為了使包括卡利基金在內之多邊機制能良好運作並充實資本，目前草擬中之諒解備忘錄應繼續適用，且出資者應根據本決議，就諒解備忘錄進行中之程序獲得適當通知；","html":"<p>44. <strong>認為</strong>為了使包括卡利基金在內之多邊機制能良好運作並充實資本，目前草擬中之諒解備忘錄應繼續適用，且出資者應根據本決議，就諒解備忘錄進行中之程序獲得適當通知；</p>","en":[11]},{"md":"45. 亦**決定**，在確保其於多邊機制運作中之職責所需之情況下，指導委員會得對諒解備忘錄以外之作業文件進行修改，且不損害法律專家小組工作成果之效力；","html":"<p>45. 亦<strong>決定</strong>，在確保其於多邊機制運作中之職責所需之情況下，指導委員會得對諒解備忘錄以外之作業文件進行修改，且不損害法律專家小組工作成果之效力；</p>","en":[12]},{"md":"IV\n審查方法論","html":"<p>IV<br />\n審查方法論</p>","en":[13,14]},{"md":"46. **決定**僅為進行包括卡利基金在內之多邊機制有效性之首次審查之目的，而實施審查方法論$^5$，並旨在於第二次有效性審查前修訂此方法論，同時**決定**假設不應作為方法論的一部分，而應作為審查的一部分進行評估；","html":"<p>46. <strong>決定</strong>僅為進行包括卡利基金在內之多邊機制有效性之首次審查之目的，而實施審查方法論<sup>5</sup>，並旨在於第二次有效性審查前修訂此方法論，同時<strong>決定</strong>假設不應作為方法論的一部分，而應作為審查的一部分進行評估；</p>","en":[15]},{"md":"---\n$^5$ CBD/COP/17/2 第 11 項附件 III","html":"<hr />\n<p><sup>5</sup> CBD/COP/17/2 第 11 項附件 III</p>","en":[16,17]}]},{"p":"p008","zh":"CBD_documents/zh/6ae530b7f82f19ef123c7a78/p008.md","en":[{"t":"President’s text on item 11"},{"t":"47. Requests that the Executive Secretary, in consultation with the Steering Committee, in line with the review methodology and subject to the availability of resources to:"},{"t":"(a) Develop and disseminate a survey available in all official languages of the United Nations to collect relevant data and information from Parties, other Governments, indigenous peoples and local communities, women and youth organizations and other relevant stakeholders and organizations, including the scientific community, database managers and the private sector, in order to inform the first review of the effectiveness of the Multilateral Mechanism, including the Cali Fund, and the development of surveys for future reviews;"},{"t":"(b)     Commission a review report containing:"},{"t":"(i)     an analysis of data and information submitted pursuant to subparagraph 58 (a) above that is in line with the pillars and governance assessment of the Multilateral Mechanism, including the Cali Fund, information from the global report on collective progress in the implementation of the Framework and other readily available sources, as relevant; and"},{"t":"(ii)    recommendations for improving the effectiveness of the Multilateral Mechanism, including the Cali Fund;"},{"t":"(c) Submit the review report to the Steering Committee to give it the opportunity to share its views and give any recommendations that it may have thereon;"},{"t":"48.       Invites the actors concerned to respond to the survey mentioned in subparagraph 47 (a) above;"},{"t":"V"},{"t":"Support for the operationalization of the Mechanism"},{"t":"49. Invites Parties with users in their jurisdiction to take measures to encourage those users to contribute to the global fund in line with the modalities of the Multilateral Mechanism, as appropriate within their national context in accordance with decision 16/2;"},{"t":"50. Calls upon Parties, and invites other Governments, relevant organizations and stakeholders, including the private sector, to organize participatory activities and partnerships, as appropriate, in order to encourage private sector engagement with and contributions to the Cali Fund and non-monetary benefit-sharing consistent with decision 16/2;"},{"t":"63. Requests Parties, and invites other Governments and relevant organizations, to support the work of the Steering Committee of the Multilateral Mechanism, including the Cali Fund, and the Secretariat of the Convention on Biological Diversity 6 acting as the interim Secretariat of the Mechanism, including the Cali Fund, through financial support and formal and informal activities such as workshops on the operationalization of the Mechanism, including the Cali Fund, and related items to continue supporting the effective participation in the work of the Committee of members from developing country Parties, in particular the least developed countries and the small island developing States among them;"},{"t":"64. Requests the Executive Secretary to enhance cooperation with the Secretariats of other relevant international organizations and bodies to promote mutual supportiveness in order to address common challenges;"},{"t":"6 United Nations, Treaty Series, vol. 1760, No. 30619."},{"t":"8/10"}],"blocks":[{"md":"主席關於議程第 11 項之文本","html":"<p>主席關於議程第 11 項之文本</p>","en":[0]},{"md":"47. **請求**執行秘書在諮詢指導委員會之情況下，根據審核方法論並在資源可用的前提下：\n    (a) 開發並發布一份以聯合國所有官方語言呈現的調查問卷，用以從締約方、其他政府、原住民族與地方社區、女性與青年組織，以及其他相關利害關係人與組織（包括科學界、資料庫管理員及私營部門）收集相關資料與資訊，以作為多邊機制（包括卡利基金）成效第一次審核以及未來審核調查開發之參考；\n    (b) 委託編製一份審核報告，其中包含：\n        (i) 針對根據上述第 58 (a) 小節所提交之資料與資訊進行分析，且該分析應與多邊機制（包括卡利基金）之支柱與治理評估一致，並視情況納入關於執行綱要集體進展之全球報告資訊及其他易於取得之來源；以及\n        (ii) 關於提升多邊機制（包括卡利基金）成效之建議；\n    (c) 將審核報告提交至指導委員會，以使其有機會分享其觀點並提出任何可能之建議；","html":"<p>47. <strong>請求</strong>執行秘書在諮詢指導委員會之情況下，根據審核方法論並在資源可用的前提下：<br />\n    (a) 開發並發布一份以聯合國所有官方語言呈現的調查問卷，用以從締約方、其他政府、原住民族與地方社區、女性與青年組織，以及其他相關利害關係人與組織（包括科學界、資料庫管理員及私營部門）收集相關資料與資訊，以作為多邊機制（包括卡利基金）成效第一次審核以及未來審核調查開發之參考；<br />\n    (b) 委託編製一份審核報告，其中包含：<br />\n        (i) 針對根據上述第 58 (a) 小節所提交之資料與資訊進行分析，且該分析應與多邊機制（包括卡利基金）之支柱與治理評估一致，並視情況納入關於執行綱要集體進展之全球報告資訊及其他易於取得之來源；以及<br />\n        (ii) 關於提升多邊機制（包括卡利基金）成效之建議；<br />\n    (c) 將審核報告提交至指導委員會，以使其有機會分享其觀點並提出任何可能之建議；</p>","en":[1,2,3,4,5]},{"md":"48. **邀請**相關行為者回應上述第 47 (a) 小節所述之調查問卷；","html":"<p>48. <strong>邀請</strong>相關行為者回應上述第 47 (a) 小節所述之調查問卷；</p>","en":[6,7,8]},{"md":"V\n對機制運作之支持","html":"<p>V<br />\n對機制運作之支持</p>","en":[9]},{"md":"49. **邀請**在其管轄範圍內設有使用者之締約方，採取適當措施以鼓勵該等使用者根據多邊機制之模式，並在其國家情境下，依照決議 16/2 向全球基金做出貢獻；","html":"<p>49. <strong>邀請</strong>在其管轄範圍內設有使用者之締約方，採取適當措施以鼓勵該等使用者根據多邊機制之模式，並在其國家情境下，依照決議 16/2 向全球基金做出貢獻；</p>","en":[10]},{"md":"50. **呼籲**締約方，並**邀請**其他政府、相關組織與利害關係人（包括私營部門），在適當情況下組織參與式活動與夥伴關係，以鼓勵私營部門參與卡利基金並對其做出貢獻，以及進行符合決議 16/2 之非貨幣性利益分享；","html":"<p>50. <strong>呼籲</strong>締約方，並<strong>邀請</strong>其他政府、相關組織與利害關係人（包括私營部門），在適當情況下組織參與式活動與夥伴關係，以鼓勵私營部門參與卡利基金並對其做出貢獻，以及進行符合決議 16/2 之非貨幣性利益分享；</p>","en":[11]},{"md":"63. **請求**締約方，並**邀請**其他政府與相關組織，透過財務支持以及正式與非正式活動（例如關於機制（包括卡利基金）運作之工作坊及相關項目），支持多邊機制（包括卡利基金）指導委員會以及擔任該機制（包括卡利基金）臨時秘書處之生物多樣性公約秘書處之工作，以持續支持開發中國家締約方成員（特別是其中的低度開發國家與小島嶼開發中國家）有效參與委員會之工作；","html":"<p>63. <strong>請求</strong>締約方，並<strong>邀請</strong>其他政府與相關組織，透過財務支持以及正式與非正式活動（例如關於機制（包括卡利基金）運作之工作坊及相關項目），支持多邊機制（包括卡利基金）指導委員會以及擔任該機制（包括卡利基金）臨時秘書處之生物多樣性公約秘書處之工作，以持續支持開發中國家締約方成員（特別是其中的低度開發國家與小島嶼開發中國家）有效參與委員會之工作；</p>","en":[12]},{"md":"64. **請求**執行秘書加強與其他相關國際組織及機構秘書處之合作，以促進相互支持，從而應對共同挑戰；","html":"<p>64. <strong>請求</strong>執行秘書加強與其他相關國際組織及機構秘書處之合作，以促進相互支持，從而應對共同挑戰；</p>","en":[13]},{"md":"---\n⁶ 聯合國，條約集，第 1760 卷，第 30619 號。","html":"<hr />\n<p>⁶ 聯合國，條約集，第 1760 卷，第 30619 號。</p>","en":[14,15]}]},{"p":"p009","zh":"CBD_documents/zh/6ae530b7f82f19ef123c7a78/p009.md","en":[{"t":"President’s text on item 11"},{"t":"Annex I"},{"t":"Terms of reference for the Ad Hoc Technical Expert Group on Allocation"},{"t":"Methodology"},{"t":"1     The Ad Hoc Technical Expert Group on Allocation Methodology is to provide technical advice","tb":1},{"t":"and guidance on the allocation methodology(ies) for disbursing funding, as decided in the annex to decision 16/2 from the global fund, to:"},{"t":"(a) governments in developing country Parties (paragraph 18 of the annex to decision 16/2), on the basis of the work of the Ad Hoc Technical Expert Group on Allocation Methodology7 and taking into consideration the recommendations for future work;"},{"t":"(b) indigenous peoples and local communities, including women and youth within those communities (paragraph 21 of the annex to decision 16/2), on the basis of the report mentioned above as well as other relevant sources, including discussions with the Steering Committee;"},{"t":"2.    The Group is to submit its report to the subsidiary body on implementation, with the view to make recommendations to the Conference of the Parties at its eighteenth meeting;"},{"t":"3.     The Technical Expert Group will comprise technical experts, as follows: 15 nominated by Parties, 7 nominated by representatives of indigenous peoples and local communities from the seven sociocultural regions, and 4 nominated by relevant organizations. The Executive Secretary, in consultation with the Bureau, will select experts on the basis of nominations received, taking gender and the relevant technical expertise of the candidates into account and applying the procedure for avoiding or managing conflicts of interest set out in the annex to decision 14/33, as amended in decision 16/26."},{"t":" 4     The Technical Expert Group may draw on existing expertise and liaise with relevant\n organizations, as appropriate, in the execution of its mandate.\n5     The Technical Expert Group may consider, inter alia, the following:","tb":1},{"t":"(a) With regard to criterion (a), develop an indicator specifically addressing species richness and biodiversity, taking into account biological diversity; territorial extent and the extent of natural ecosystems; ecosystem diversity, including ecological distinctiveness; endemism; ecological integrity and connectivity; and biodiversity conserved and sustainably used by Indigenous Peoples and local communities, including in their lands and territories;"},{"t":"(b) With regard to criterion (b), reformulate the indicator to clearly reflect the country of origin of the genetic resources from which the digital sequence information on genetic resources was derived, rather than the country in which the digital sequence information on genetic resources was generated or uploaded to a database;"},{"t":"(c) With regard to criterion (c), develop an indicator based on information available in National Biodiversity Strategies and Action Plans (NBSAPs) and national capacity-development plans, reflecting capacity needs for the conservation and sustainable use of biodiversity, taking into account the circumstances of developing country Parties, in particular least developed countries and small island developing States, Parties with economies in transition, megadiverse developing country Parties, in particular least developed countries and small island developing States, Parties with economies in transition, megadiverse developing countries, and the needs of indigenous peoples and local communities, while avoiding indicators that merely reflect the economic development or payment capacity of Parties."},{"t":"7 CBD/DSI/AHTEG/2026/2/3"},{"t":"9/10"}],"blocks":[{"md":"主席關於議程第 11 項之文本","html":"<p>主席關於議程第 11 項之文本</p>","en":[0,1]},{"md":"附件 I\n分配方法論特設技術專家小組職權範圍","html":"<p>附件 I<br />\n分配方法論特設技術專家小組職權範圍</p>","en":[2,3]},{"md":"1.\n分配方法論特設技術專家小組應針對如決議 16/2 附件所決定，從全球基金撥付資金之分配方法論，提供技術建議與指引，對象包括：\n(a) 開發中國家締約方之政府（決議 16/2 附件第 18 段），其基礎應基於分配方法論特設技術專家小組$^7$之工作，並考量未來工作之建議；\n(b) 原住民族與地方社區，包括該等社區內之女性與青年（決議 16/2 附件第 21 段），其基礎應基於上述報告以及其他相關來源，包括與指導委員會之討論；","html":"<p>1.<br />\n分配方法論特設技術專家小組應針對如決議 16/2 附件所決定，從全球基金撥付資金之分配方法論，提供技術建議與指引，對象包括：<br />\n(a) 開發中國家締約方之政府（決議 16/2 附件第 18 段），其基礎應基於分配方法論特設技術專家小組<sup>7</sup>之工作，並考量未來工作之建議；<br />\n(b) 原住民族與地方社區，包括該等社區內之女性與青年（決議 16/2 附件第 21 段），其基礎應基於上述報告以及其他相關來源，包括與指導委員會之討論；</p>","en":[4,5,6,7]},{"md":"2.\n本小組應向執行附屬機構提交其報告，旨在向第十八次締約方大會提出建議；","html":"<p>2.<br />\n本小組應向執行附屬機構提交其報告，旨在向第十八次締約方大會提出建議；</p>","en":[8]},{"md":"3.\n技術專家小組應由下列技術專家組成：15 名由締約方提名，7 名由來自七個社會文化區域之原住民族與地方社區代表提名，以及 4 名由相關組織提名。執行秘書應在諮詢主席團後，根據收到的提名，在考慮候選人之性別與相關技術專業，並適用決議 16/26 修訂後之決議 14/33 附件所載之避免或管理利益衝突程序之基礎上，選任專家。","html":"<p>3.<br />\n技術專家小組應由下列技術專家組成：15 名由締約方提名，7 名由來自七個社會文化區域之原住民族與地方社區代表提名，以及 4 名由相關組織提名。執行秘書應在諮詢主席團後，根據收到的提名，在考慮候選人之性別與相關技術專業，並適用決議 16/26 修訂後之決議 14/33 附件所載之避免或管理利益衝突程序之基礎上，選任專家。</p>","en":[9]},{"md":"4.\n技術專家小組在執行其職責時，得視情況利用現有專業知識，並與相關組織進行聯繫。","html":"<p>4.<br />\n技術專家小組在執行其職責時，得視情況利用現有專業知識，並與相關組織進行聯繫。</p>","en":[10]},{"md":"5.\n技術專家小組可考慮（除其他事項外）下列事項：","html":"<p>5.<br />\n技術專家小組可考慮（除其他事項外）下列事項：</p>","en":[10]},{"md":"(a) 針對標準 (a)，開發一項專門針對物種豐富度與生物多樣性之指標，並考量生物多樣性；領土範圍與自然生態系之範圍；生態系多樣性（包括生態獨特性）；特有性；生態完整性與連結性；以及由原住民族與地方社區（包括在其土地與領土內）所保育且永續利用之生物多樣性；\n(b) 針對標準 (b)，重新制定指標，以清楚反映遺傳資源數位序列資訊所衍生之遺傳資源來源國，而非產生或上傳至資料庫之遺傳資源數位序列資訊所在國；\n(c) 針對標準 (c)，開發一項基於國家生物多樣性策略與行動計畫 (NBSAPs) 及國家能力建構計畫中可用資訊之指標，以反映生物多樣性保育與永續利用之能力需求，並考量開發中國家締約方（特別是低度開發國家與小島嶼開發中國家）、經濟轉型中締約方、生物多樣性極豐富之開發中國家，以及原住民族與地方社區之需求，同時避免使用僅反映締約方經濟發展或支付能力之指標。","html":"<p>(a) 針對標準 (a)，開發一項專門針對物種豐富度與生物多樣性之指標，並考量生物多樣性；領土範圍與自然生態系之範圍；生態系多樣性（包括生態獨特性）；特有性；生態完整性與連結性；以及由原住民族與地方社區（包括在其土地與領土內）所保育且永續利用之生物多樣性；<br />\n(b) 針對標準 (b)，重新制定指標，以清楚反映遺傳資源數位序列資訊所衍生之遺傳資源來源國，而非產生或上傳至資料庫之遺傳資源數位序列資訊所在國；<br />\n(c) 針對標準 (c)，開發一項基於國家生物多樣性策略與行動計畫 (NBSAPs) 及國家能力建構計畫中可用資訊之指標，以反映生物多樣性保育與永續利用之能力需求，並考量開發中國家締約方（特別是低度開發國家與小島嶼開發中國家）、經濟轉型中締約方、生物多樣性極豐富之開發中國家，以及原住民族與地方社區之需求，同時避免使用僅反映締約方經濟發展或支付能力之指標。</p>","en":[11,12,13]},{"md":"---\n$^7$ CBD/DSI/AHTEG/2026/2/3","html":"<hr />\n<p><sup>7</sup> CBD/DSI/AHTEG/2026/2/3</p>","en":[14,15]}]},{"p":"p010","zh":"CBD_documents/zh/6ae530b7f82f19ef123c7a78/p010.md","en":[{"t":"President’s text on item 11"},{"t":"6.    Subject to the availability of financial resources, the Ad Hoc Technical Expert Group will meet, as needed, to ensure the timely provision of advice and, wherever possible, back-to-back with other relevant meetings. Where possible, the Secretariat will use available means of electronic communication to reduce the need for in-person meetings."},{"t":"__________"},{"t":"10/10"}],"blocks":[{"md":"主席關於議程第 11 項之文本","html":"<p>主席關於議程第 11 項之文本</p>","en":[0]},{"md":"6.\n在財務資源可用的情況下，特設技術專家小組將視需要召開會議，以確保及時提供建議，並在可能的情況下，與其他相關會議接續舉行。在可能的情況下，秘書處將利用現有的電子通訊手段，以減少實體會議的需求。","html":"<p>6.<br />\n在財務資源可用的情況下，特設技術專家小組將視需要召開會議，以確保及時提供建議，並在可能的情況下，與其他相關會議接續舉行。在可能的情況下，秘書處將利用現有的電子通訊手段，以減少實體會議的需求。</p>","en":[1,2,3]}]}]};
